<title>Palpable Abdominal Mass: Diagnosis.</title>
<graphic href="eee0161-w001.gif" />
<cell type="start" id="cell-1">
<label>What is the location of the palpable abdominal mass?</label>
<path target="cell-2">Upper abdomen</path>
<path target="cell-3">Lower abdomen</path>
<path target="cell-4">Midline</path>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-2">
<label>Is hematemesis present?</label>
<path target="cell-5">Yes</path>
<path target="cell-6">No</path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-5">
<label>Perform upper GI endoscopy Mass identified?</label>
<path target="cell-8">Yes</path>
<path target="cell-6">No</path>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-6">
<label>Perform CT of abdomen Mass identified?</label>
<path target="cell-8">Yes</path>
<path target="cell-7">No</path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-7">
<label>Follow clinically</label>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-8">
<label>Treat cause.</label>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-3">
<label>Is pregnancy suspected?</label>
<path target="cell-9">Yes</path>
<path target="cell-10">No</path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-9">
<label>Order ultrasound of abdomen, pelvis</label>
<path target="cell-11"></path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-11">
<label>Pregnancy found?</label>
<path target="cell-10">No</path>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-10">
<label>Is hematochezia present?</label>
<path target="cell-12">Yes</path>
<path target="cell-13">No</path>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-12">
<label>Perform colonoscopy Mass identified?</label>
<path target="cell-8">Yes</path>
<path target="cell-13">No</path>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-13">
<label>Perform US or CT of abdomen with oral and IV contrast. If US chosen but indeterminate, follow with CT. MRI also an option. Mass identified?</label>
<path target="cell-8">Yes</path>
<path target="cell-7">No</path>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-4">
<label>Is mass pulsatile?</label>
<path target="cell-14">Yes</path>
<path target="cell-15">No</path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-14">
<label>Perform screening ultrasound of abdominal aorta If positive, perform CTA to define aortic anatomy better.</label>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-15">
<label>Protuberant, reducible, + bowel sounds over mass?</label>
<path target="cell-16">Yes</path>
<path target="cell-17">No</path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-16">
<label>Hernia (ventral, umbilical, diastasis recti).</label>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-17">
<label>Suprapubic location; Passage of Foley catheter reduces mass?</label>
<path target="cell-18">Yes</path>
<path target="cell-19">No</path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-18">
<label>Distended bladder.</label>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-19">
<label>Perform abdominal CT scan for diagnosis. Mass identified?</label>
<path target="cell-8">Yes</path>
<path target="cell-7">No</path>
</cell>
<footnotes>
<footnote>Data from American College of Radiology (ACR), Expert panel on Gastrointestinal Imaging. Imaging evaluation of the palpable abdominal mass. Reston, VA: American College of Radiology (ACR); 2001. 2 p. </footnote>
</footnotes>
</algorithm>
